<table width="758" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="10" height="100%" align="center">
  <tr> 
    <td bgcolor="#000000" valign="top"> 
      <div align="center"> 
        <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="25">
          <tr> 
            <td valign="top" width="50%"> 
              <table width="100%" border="1" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="5" bordercolor="#10131B">
                <tr> 
                  <td bgcolor="#10131B"> 
                    <div align="center"><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b><font color="gold">Attendance 
                      Promotion System</font></b></font></div>
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr> 
                  <td bgcolor="#000000"> 
                    <p><font size="2" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#e1e1e1">Loot 
                      decisions, and other merits, would be based off what is 
                      most important to this guild, your overall attendance and 
                      contribution to the guild. Sounds like DKP so far, but it 
                      isn't. There are many distinct differences that we will 
                      outline below.</font></p>
                    <p><font size="2" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#e1e1e1"> 
                      You will be awarded Attendance Points (AP) for your time 
                      spent on raids, present and participating (not AFK/Asleep), 
                      based around a points per mob / clearance (i.e. Tunare) 
                      system. The raids that give Attendance Points are specified 
                      in our &quot;Hit List&quot;. Attendance Points can also 
                      be gained by completing goals from the list of goal opportunities 
                      provided by the officers (i.e. Emperor Key Completion). 
                      We expect nothing less than for our members to avoid making 
                      enormous mistakes. You will be penalized, by removal of 
                      an amount of Attendance Points, if you cost the guild time 
                      through major errors that are beyond a guild of this caliber.</font></p>
                    <p><font size="2" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#e1e1e1"> 
                      We maintain a daily updated database list that is displayed 
                      on our website roster. It shows your total Attendance Points, 
                      Monthly Attendance Points, a list of all items you have 
                      received and their worth by clicking on a member's name, 
                      and a list of every raid you have attended and received 
                      points for. There is a bonus modifier to the raid points 
                      for people that play outside of North America, because for 
                      them it is much more of a struggle to raid on our time schedule. 
                      Points are split into two categories, overall and monthly. 
                      Overall Attendance Points are primarily used to decide decisions 
                      on loot distribution.</font></p>
                    <p><font size="2" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#e1e1e1"> 
                      When an item drops, anyone that wants to be considered for 
                      it would tell the designated Loot Council member with what 
                      they have in the current slot and a request to be considered. 
                      Each item (of significant worth) has a point value designating 
                      its amount of worth in Attendance Points. When you are awarded 
                      an item, the value of that item is added to your Accumulated 
                      Loot Points forcing your Attendance Credit to decrease (Attendance 
                      Points - Accumulated Loot Points = Attendance Credit). The 
                      item you are currently using in that slot would be taken 
                      into consideration when deciding the loot. When you ask 
                      for an item, the value of your current item is temporarily 
                      deducted from your points (only for this decision), and 
                      the totals would be presented to the loot council. The person 
                      with the most points would be awarded the item (example 
                      below). Overall Attendance Points are looked at when deciding 
                      awards.</font></p>
                    <p><font size="2" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#e1e1e1"> 
                      This is different from DKP in many ways. Items would never 
                      rot because noone thinks they are worth &quot;spending&quot; 
                      points on. People cannot purchase items for their twinks 
                      (twink is not an alt) if someone's main character in our 
                      guild needs it and it able to loot, and anything droppable 
                      that noone can use will go to guild bank. You CANNOT spend 
                      points on an item for a twink if it's droppable. If you 
                      run out of points then you have had your share of loots 
                      for your time that you have invested into the guild and 
                      someone else would get the item that hasn't received their 
                      share. If no one asks for the item because it isn't a big 
                      enough upgrade for anyone or because no one wants to lose 
                      Overall Attendance Credit to be awarded the item then the 
                      item will offered to purchase for twinks ONLY if the item 
                      is no drop. This gives you the ability to gain items for 
                      your twinks using your main character. If no one wants to 
                      spend points on getting their twink an item, then it will 
                      rot. We do not have time to make an issue out of twink gear. 
                      We will NEVER hold up a raid to wait for you to bring your 
                      twink to loot. We would move on and if you can get your 
                      twink there while we do our shit, grats you. If this becomes 
                      an issue, we will remove this opportunity. Also, if we find 
                      out that people are multi-playing characters on raids to 
                      get them both Attendance Points, they would be penalized 
                      harshly. If you are botting a character, you need to tell 
                      us. If this gets out of hand (dishonesty) it can result 
                      in guild removal.</font></p>
                    <p><font size="2" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#e1e1e1"> 
                      We can now offer you the ability to gear your secondary 
                      character (ALT) if he / she is used on raids to benefit 
                      the guild based on the following requirements. The ALT must 
                      be level 61 with a minimum of 6 Alternate Advancement points. 
                      The ALT must do his / her job when attending raids to keep 
                      the ALT status for AP. At any time will an ALT be removed 
                      from AP privelage if he / she is not doing his / her job 
                      to help the guild. Only one ALT per main will be allowed 
                      to achieve AP and that ALT must come to at least 95% of 
                      all raids the primary character attends. You must use two 
                      different computers if you are playing an alternate character 
                      at raids, we will NOT tolerate EQWindows, it does not get 
                      the job done when you can't see both characters at once. 
                      <b>The maximum and ALT can earn at raids is 90% of the current 
                      raid AP</b> mainly because the ALT isn't focused on 100%. 
                      The ALT must be approved by the guild leader before being 
                      allowed 90% AP rights. No ALTs are allowed new member AP, 
                      when you begin receiving AP for your ALT you start at <strong>0</strong>. 
                      Any keys (Emp, VT, etc) that give AP the ALT will receive 
                      half AP only for the keys completed. We have discovered, 
                      through research, that ALTs help the success of this guild 
                      and we need to keep them geared with the rest of the guild 
                      if we're going to move up to more challenging events.</font></p>
                    <p><font size="2" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#e1e1e1"> 
                      When we started &lt;Vindictive&gt;, it was meant to be a 
                      raiding guild with required attendance. We have had problems 
                      with attendance in the past and this system has worked wonders. 
                      As an addition to all of this, you will be required to produce 
                      a certain number of Attendance Points per month. If you 
                      cannot meet this goal, on an average monthly basis, then 
                      you should not be a member of &lt;Vindictive&gt;. (For example, 
                      if the goal is 30 AP a month, and you made 45 one month 
                      then 15 the next, your average would be 30. This is acceptable.) 
                      We feel this policy reflects what we want in guild members 
                      and gives an incentive to attend on time and stay during 
                      raids.</font></p>
                    </td>
                </tr>
              </table>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        
